{
  "$comment": "How a device downsamples local remaining-quota samples into uploadable buckets (`bucket`) and how several devices' buckets merge into the one series an Account read draws (`merge`). Bucket size is 900 s when the window's duration_seconds is at most 86 400, otherwise 3 600 s; bucket_start is floor(observed_at / size) × size in UTC; a bucket's value is the maximum used_percent in it for that resets_at; a bucket whose value equals the previous uploaded bucket of the same (window, resets_at) is not sent; a new resets_at is a new series. The span of a window is min(30 d, max(48 h, 4 × duration_seconds)): five-hour → 48 h, weekly → 28 d, monthly → 30 d. Points older than that span are not uploaded; a series with no duration_seconds is refused. Merge takes the maximum used_percent per (window_id, resets_at, bucket_start), oldest first. Shape is JSON only: TypeScript (`packages/quota-model`), Swift, and Rust each answer this file. See ADR 0062. The fold a surface draws is still quota-history-conformance.json.",
